{
  "id": "blocker-repair",
  "name": "blocker_repair",
  "description": "Repair the deliverable's blocker rows, cheapest-and-safest first. Pass 1 substitutes each rule's forbidden form with its canonical one, touching only the offending span. Pass 2 re-translates ONLY what substitution cannot fix — structural defects such as a repeated token, where the objection is word order rather than a term. The order matters: free re-translation takes the licence it is given, and when it repaired all 30 rows at once it cleared every rule while dropping 방출 from a SPECT term and swapping a DEXA term for an unrelated one, neither of which any detector watches. Substitution cannot do that. Adoption is still gated: only rows whose blocker actually clears are kept, and the patch-safety gate independently refuses any change introducing a new blocker. Re-promotes ko_imaging_deliverable.",
